[Music]  welcome back to curious archive this  video is the second part of a two-part  series exploring the incredible  speculative biology project of snyad a  planet teeming with incredible alien  life snyde was created by cm koziman an  exceptional artist and the creator of  all tomorrows and as usual i have links  below where you can follow and support  his work when we left off we'd visited  many of the basic life forms on snyad  now it's time to study aliens of greater  sizes and stranger biology in a journey  that will reveal secrets from snyad's  mysterious past and perhaps its  unexpected future with humans and even  some never-before-seen images from  kozaman's upcoming book so let's get  started  beginning on the curious island of mapag  something on the beaches is walking  upright on two legs this is an armless  bloomberman a creature whose facial  pouch in which it is currently carrying  its baby is so pronounced it looks  almost humanoid are the armless  bloomberman snyad's approximation of  intelligent life not quite these bipedal  oddities are actually closer to earth  penguins than they are to us as they're  cumbersome on land but better adapted  for the water but the intelligence of  these creatures isn't distinct from  other animals on snyad indeed the author  imagines no species currently living on  the planet's surface possess advanced  intellect but looking into the  archaeological record of snyad there's  evidence that intelligence may have  existed in the distant past according to  cozumen 30 million year old stone axe  heads have been discovered but there's  no clues as to their origins and  metallic artifacts of an apparently  artificial nature called the decided  screws have been dated to even earlier  as snyat is almost twice as old as earth  it seems that perhaps civilization has  risen multiple times only to be  obliterated and erased by mass  extinctions but all this is uncertain  the creatures that currently wander  across nyad however are truly  fascinating regardless of their  intelligence on numerous offshore  islands the beaches are buzzing with the  sounds of grey bloombermen a related  type of bloomba miniform like their  larger cousins these somewhat awkward  looking creatures are also most graceful  under the waves able to chase down  numerous marine organisms almost like  tiny seals hilariously kozaman mentions  the grey bloomberman will one day become  a major symbol in the popular culture of  human settlers and will even form the  basis for cartoon characters and  children's toys that's right humans will  eventually create settlements on snyad  khozman states that in the future of  this narrative human history will become  intertwined with that of snyads as we  create the first settlements on this  alien world  the idea of humans trying to coexist  with these awe-inspiring yet often  terrifying creatures is certainly an  interesting one and one of the most  important future animals to human  settlers is the orca runners mighty  herbivores with distinctive coloring and  a peaceful demeanor thanks to their fast  running speeds and friendly temperament  these unusual creatures will  surprisingly become critical  domesticated animals similar to horses  in the lives of these first settlers  this is a telltale sign that humans and  the planet's fantastical native life  will have a wide range of surprising  interactions  on the subject of fantastical life the  windy crags of the pontic mountains  conceal one of snyad's most spectacular  animals the aptly named spineys possess  four claws first head beaks and dorsal  spines all elongated into javelin-like  spikes despite appearances however the  spineys are herbivorous and have evolved  these spikes purely for defense so  they're actually closer to a hedgehog  than they are to some apex super  predator kozaman imagines human  colonists rarely glimpse spines due to  their shyness instead only hearing the  haunting sounds they produce by rattling  their spikes against each other across  the mainland continent a hulking armored  lifeform is on the move this is the  chasmatorus a type of alatora form an  extremely successful lineage of large  snyaty herbivores unlike its more  amiable cousins however chasmatorus  prefers to be left alone and will charge  down and trample anything that invades  its territory much like an earth  rhinoceros and since they grow to 22  feet or seven meters long their poor  attitude will make them difficult for  colonists to study  in the misty forests of midland a much  smaller organism wanders among the trees  the austro-taurus is an alatora form  which has shrunk considerably due to its  forest habitat and rarely exceeds six  feet or two meters in length far from  defenseless the ostrotorus has evolved  armadillo-like bands of segmented body  armor which keeps the tiny titans safe  from predators like the futatora forms  in all manner of biomes across snyad you  might find that futura forms on the  prowl this particular species is an  arbophobis an animal whose name alludes  to its tree climbing abilities but is  indeed able to conquer most any  environment like most fututura forms  arbophobis is an agile adaptive hunter  similar in many respects to the large  cat species of our own planet indeed the  deadliness of this predator will end up  being its undoing as these fearless  hunters will attack countless settlers  in the early days of human exploration  and as a result the arbophobis will be  purposefully hunted to extinction  but there's another hunter early  settlers will fear even more than the  orbovobus a creature they'll know  through screams on dark knights and the  glints of its huge eyes that is until  cameras reveal these nocturnal organisms  are barely over three feet or one meter  long  called inferno kions these timid hunters  don't deserve their frightening name as  they only use their scissor-like jaws to  feed on small nighttime animals and  simply have unusually loud coals and  large eyes for their body size  in the nearby peaks of oro land a close  relative lives in seclusion these are  the selena khan the largest species of  their order and a critically endangered  one cozumen notes they often hunt near  forest streams at dusk with the starry  sky reflecting off their enormous  haunting eyes it will be a truly sad  loss if these fascinating animals fade  into extinction sometime in snyd's  future  one species with a far more certain  future can be found in abundance north  of the divider mountains this is a  pescadon a bipedal omnivore with a  curious penchant for cooperation one of  the most social animals on snyad  pescadons are known to coordinate hunts  in large family groups with similar  dynamics to wolf packs on earth their  affinity towards social bonding will  make them a favorite domesticated animal  among future human settlers with their  path mirroring that of humans and dogs  if dogs were 10 feet or 3 meters long  that is  upon the elevated plateaus of the  southeast another animal that will have  a key role in humanity's future is  waiting these bizarre spherical  creatures whose first head faces have  become mashed directly into their bodies  are actually the cousins of the  pescodons we just visited and indeed  these hulking heavy beasts are of a  similar size which will make them ideal  draft animals filling a role similar to  earth cows and the lives of the first  settlers  and speaking of early settlers during  the first aerial surveys of snyad vast  paths along the landscape will be  glimpsed and at first assumed to be the  creation of intelligent life in reality  however these lines are the trails of  the unintelligent tractor snakes massive  herbivores of the lofofid classification  who vacuum the land for vegetation like  living combine harvesters at an  astonishing 22 feet or seven meters long  these giants might not be great thinkers  but they're truly impressive shapers of  their environment  at the edge of the enchirion desert a  more modest-sized relative slithers  across the sands this is a phytophyton a  lifeform that at first glance shows a  high degree of convergent evolution with  snakes here on earth unlike all types of  snakes we're familiar with however the  phytophyton isn't a hunter but instead a  generalist herbivore like their larger  tractor snake cousins  if you're looking for a carnivorous  snake analog the sprog land along the  eastern plains contains the closest  thing on snyad say hello to a  chasmatomos a rather odd looking fellow  that is a representative of the poorly  understood sprago fighting  classification while a predator at only  7 inches or 20 centimeters long they're  not the most frightening thing on snyad  yet they do have one truly fascinating  adaptation the ability to shed their  fatty tails when attacked in a strategy  not dissimilar from some types of geckos  unlike geckos however chesmatomo's tales  don't grow back  we've now seen species from all over  snyad and have learned about the future  role they'll play in the lives of human  settlers but there's still one great  frontier we've yet to chart the massive  planetary oceans  taking the common jet shark as our  baseline for underwater life we'll see  the path of life in the oceans is vastly  different from on land the group the jet  shark belongs to the ghetto sets take  the two-headed sniaty body plan in a  highly unexpected direction their first  heads are actually connected to their  digestive tract and their second heads  have become an almost jet like pump  connected to an entirely different  system that's right much of undersea  sniaty life is jet powered kind of like  some species of squids on earth just  taken to a new extreme the jet shark has  found unsurprisingly a niche similar to  a shark in the underwater food chain  but far to the north in the frigid polar  waters you can find a very different  kind of undersea giant meet the  hedrocetoids a 22 feet or 7 meter long  life form that is similarly jet powered  protected from the cold with layers of  thick blubber they travel in large  family pods much like the mighty orcas  that swim through our own oceans unlike  the predacious orcas however the  hadrocetoids are peaceful filter feeders  and elsewhere in the ocean the fantastic  conclusion to our tour of life on snyad  is waiting the xenoposeidon  thalassacaros is a truly awe-inspiring  beast and the largest animal on the  planet at a staggering 130 feet or 40  meters in length their cavernous beaks  have an ingenious system of inlets and  holes that allow them to filter huge  amounts of plankton from the water  giving them the food they need to reach  such incredible sizes of course these  creatures are most similar to earth  whales and their size and feeding  behavior but what relationship will  future humans have with this animal  that's a detail the author has yet to  reveal  indeed many more details regarding snyad  might be revealed later as kozman is  working on a meticulous remake of the  project which thus far has yielded some  incredible reimaginings of familiar  sniadi organisms he gave me a few never  before seen images from the upcoming  book to share which are on the screen  now and in my opinion these new designs  are even better than the old ones so if  you're a fan of this project and like me  really want to see a book someday please  follow and support kozamin in the links  in the description below and as always  thanks for watching if you enjoyed this  entry please lend your support and like  subscribe and hit the notification icon  to stay up to date on all things curious  see you in the next video  you

